          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The “doubly supersymmetric geometric approach” (
            %a{:href => "#BPSTV95"}> Bandos, Pasti, Sorokin, Tonin &amp; Volkov 1995
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#HoweSezgin97"} Howe &amp; Sezgin 1997
            %em super-embedding approach
            (
            %a{:href => "#HoweRaetzelSezgin98"}> Howe, Raetzel &amp; Sezgin 1998
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Sorokin00"} Sorokin 2000
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            entirely within
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            is taken to be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-models"} Green-Schwarz sigma-models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            is taken to be a supermanifold, as in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NSR+string"} NSR string
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/pBraneEmbedding.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#FSS19c"} FSS 19c
          %p#SuperEmbeddingCondition
            The central observation of the super-embedding approach is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            are identified with nothing but a natural
            %strong super-embedding condition
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+co-frame+field"} super co-frame field
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetime"} superspacetime
            relative to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \Sigma \to X
            (really just:
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion"} immersion
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                on the bosonic components
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^a
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+co-frame+field"} super co-frame field
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-spacetime"} super-spacetime
                %em super-embedding condition
                is &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "#Sorokin00"}> Sorokin 2000 (4.36-37)
                ;
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "super-embedding+approach#Bandos11"} Bandos 2011 (2.6-2.9)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "super-embedding+approach#BandosSorokin23"} Bandos &amp; Sorokin 2023 (5.13-14)
                = succeed "&rbrack;:" do
                  %a{:href => "super-embedding+formalism#BPSTV95"} Bandos et al. 1995 (2.23)
              #eq:BosonicSuperEmbeddingCondition.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mi a
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mtext for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi a
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi p
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mtext for
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi a
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mi p
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\phi^\ast
                      \\, E^a
                      \\;\;
                      \=
                      \\;\;
                      \\left\{
                      \\,
                      \\begin{array}{l}
                      e^a &amp; \text{for}\; a \leq p
                      \\\
                      0   &amp; \text{for}\, a \gt p
                      \\mathrlap{\,,}
                      \\end{array}
                      \\right.
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^a
                are the bosonic components of the co-frame field on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi p
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1+p \coloneqq dim(\Sigma)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension
                of its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                bosonic
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} manifold
            %li
              %p
                on the fermionic components
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+co-frame+field"} super co-frame field
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetime"} super spacetime
                the condition is &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "#Sorokin00"}> Sorokin 2000 (4.46)
                ;
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "#BandosSorokin23"} Bandos &amp; Sorokin 2023 (5.26)
              #eq:FermionicSuperEmbeddingCondition.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi P
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi ψ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\phi^\ast
                      \\, P \Psi
                      \\;\;
                      \=
                      \\;\;
                      \\psi
                      \\,,
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo ≔
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \coloneqq \tfrac{1}{2}(1 + \Gamma_{p+1} \cdots \Gamma_d)
                is the corresponding transversal fermionic projector and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
                are the fermionic components of the co-frame field on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
            Here we may observe &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#GSS24"}> GSS24, §2
            \&amp;rbrack; that a co-frame satisfying the bosonic “super-embedding condition”
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BosonicSuperEmbeddingCondition"} (1)
            is algebraically what is known in the mathematical literature as a (higher dimensional)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Darboux+coframe"} Darboux coframe
            for the given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion"} immersion
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Riemannian+immersion#DarbouxCoFramePullingBackToCoframeOnImmersedManifold"} there
          %p
            Crucially, the would-be fermionic Darboux-condition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mi P
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^\ast \overline{P} \Psi = 0
            is
            %em not
            imposed (analogous to how the
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            imposes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+torsion+constraint"} torsion constraint
            just on the bosonic coframe components): Remarkably, it turns out that the freedom in violating this would-be constraint accounts exactly for the presence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            on the
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            (with their
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            (with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            in the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%282%2C0%29+SCFT"} D=6 N=(2,0) SCFT
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#KappaSymmetry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            \-Symmetry as super-general covariance
          %p
            The notorious phenomenon of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kappa-symmetry"} kappa-symmetry
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-models"} Green-Schwarz sigma-models
            is revealed by the superembedding approach to be nothing but the odd-graded components of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-diffeomorphism"} super-diffeomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariance
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+covariance"} general covariance
            (
            %a{:href => "#SorokinTkachVolkov89"}> Sorokin-Tkach-Volkov 89
            , review includes
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sorokin0"} Sorokin 00, section 4.3
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#HoweSezgin04"} Howe-Sezgin 04, section 4.3
          %p If
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                denotes a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetime"} superspacetime
                locally modeled on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                denotes a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} super
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
                locally modeled on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p,1\vert \mathbf{N}/2}
            %li
              %p
                so that a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
                configuration for a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
                of shape
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                to propagate in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a morphism of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
                of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Σ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mtext super-worldvolume
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi ϕ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mtext sigma-model super-field
                            %mtd
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mtext super-spacetime
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\Sigma &amp;&amp; \text{super-worldvolume}
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi}} &amp;&amp;\text{sigma-model super-field}&amp;
                      \\\
                      X &amp;&amp; \text{super-spacetime}
                      }
          %p then:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the postcomposition
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-isometries"} super-isometries
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} X
                is in even degree the action of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
                and in odd degree the action of
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
                on the sigma-model fields;
            %li
              %p
                the precomposition action of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-diffeomorphism"} super-diffeomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \Sigma
                is in even degree the action of bosonic worldvolume
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
                and in odd degree the action of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                    \-symmetry
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                        %mtd
                          %munderover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ≃
                            %mrow
                              %mi κ
                              %mtext -symmetry
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %munderover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ≃
                            %mtext spacetime supersymmetry
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Sigma  &amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{\kappa\text{-symmetry}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Sigma
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi'}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{\text{spacetime supersymmetry}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice here the assumption that the number of odd directions on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            is half that of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            solutions are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
          %p For example, consider the embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{2,1} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{10,1}
          %p
            of 2+1d
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane"} membrane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{10,1}
            from the 11d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(10,1)
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+group"} product group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Iso(2,1) \times SO(8)
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  Iso(10,1)
          %p
            (meaning that this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
            of the embedding).
          %p
            Now consider instead
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
            (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
            the irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
            representation in 11), hence the local model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetimes"} super spacetimes
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
            preserves the embedding in that the
            %a{:href => "Majorana+spinor#TheSpinorPairingToVectors"} spinor bilinear pairing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mn 1
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\psi}_1 \Gamma \psi_2
            on that subspace lands in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2,1} \hookrightarrow Iso(2,1) \hookrightarrow Iso(10,1)
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sorokin00"}> Sorokin 2000, section 5.1
            ). This is found to be the case for a half-dimensional subspace, and hence we may lift the above to a super-embedding of the form
          #eq:M2WordvolumeInSpacetime.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
          %p
            (where now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irrep"} irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
            representation in 3d, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 8
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of 8 copies of it) such that the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            now is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 8
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Iso(\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}}) \times Spin(8)
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  Iso(\mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}})
                  \\,.
          %p
            It is in this sense that the membrane “breaks exactly half the supersymmetry”, namely from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 8
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}
          %p
            If one now thinks of this not as inclusions of global spacetimes, but of their super tangent spaces at the points where the membrane sits in spacetime, then this reflects the local structure of
            = succeed "-symmetry:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-symmetries" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Iso
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 8
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 8 \otimes \mathbf{2}} )
          %p
            This explains why
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+models"} Green-Schwarz sigma models
            is taken to quotient out precisely half the spinor components, hence why, in the fully super-covariant formulation, one takes the worldvolume of a super
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p,1\vert \mathbf{N}/2}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+models"} sigma models
            for “non-BPS super
            = succeed "-branes\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %h2#brane_lagrangians_by_relative_trivialization Brane Lagrangians by relative trivialization
          %p
            The super-embedding formalism has mostly been used for deriving
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane+sigma-models"} super p-brane sigma-models
          %p
            But at least for some brane species, also their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"} Lagrangian densities
            emerge naturally from the super-embedding, namely as relative trivializations of the brane cocycles as given by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} brane scah/brane bouquet
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BraneSuperEmbeddings.jpg", :title => ""} BraneSuperEmbeddings.jpg
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BraneSuperEmbeddings.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#HSS18"} HSS 18
          %h3#LagrangiansForStringsAndMembranes For strings and membranes
          %p
            For the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-membrane"} super-membrane
            the construction of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"} Lagrangian densities
            as relative trivialization of their super-cocycles along their super-embeddings is estalished in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HoweSezgin05"} Howe-Sezgin 05 (4.72)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#HSS18"} HSS 18, Prop. 6.10
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/M2BraneEmbedding.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
